A lacuna field thema doesn't define (severity, line 12 of 1.0).

Only the pattern constraint in thema's lacuna.cue catches it, by evaluating to
error(). The error is positioned at that call in the kernel, and the authored
position is lost entirely. checkUnknownFields, which points at the author's
line, covers lineages, schema entries and lenses, but not lacunas. A compiler
that owns the lacuna syntax can reject unknown keys itself.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
	lacuna: {
		kind: "Placeholder"
		target: "count"
		message: "count is a placeholder"
		severity: "high"
	}
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
	lacuna: {
		kind:     "Placeholder"
		target:   "count"
		message:  "count is a placeholder"
		severity: "high"
	}
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- out/error --
severity is not a field of a lacuna:
    ship/history/1.0.thema:12:13
-- out/positions --
severity is not a field of a lacuna
	authored ship/history/1.0.thema:12:13
